  "chapter": 688,
  "signer": "KATHY HOCHUL",
  "text": " \n                APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 75 Chapter 688\n \n        MEMORANDUM filed with Senate Bill Number 979-A, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT  to  amend  the real property law, in relation to requiring\n        real estate brokers to receive training in cultural competency\"\n \n    APPROVED\n \n  Under Article 12-A of the real property law, applications  for  licen-\nsure  to  be real estate salespersons or brokers require proof of having\ncompleted a fixed number of hours of real estate coursework that  covers\nseveral subject areas required by law, and renewal of licensure requires\nproof  of  having  completed twenty-two and one half hours of continuing\neducation (CE) coursework, with a minimum number of hours  dedicated  to\nidentified subject areas.\n\n  This bill would (i) add a class on cultural competency training to the\ncurriculum  for  new  licensees; and (ii) require that of the twenty-two\nand one half hours of CE relating to renewals, at  least  two  hours  of\ncultural competency training be completed.\n \n  I  support  this legislation, but have concerns that there is no defi-\nnition of the term \"cultural competency\". Therefore, I have agreed  with\nthe  legislature  to  pass legislation in the upcoming session that will\ndefine the term, \"cultural competency,\" and provide for  an  implementa-\ntion  timeframe  that reflects the operational mechanics associated with\nexpanding coursework requirements for real estate professionals.\n \n  Based upon this agreement with the  legislature,  I  am  signing  this\nbill.\n \n  This bill is approved.                         (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n \n                                ______\n",
  "year": 2021
 },
